<title>USA: Meris Labs president/CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>Meris Labs president/CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Meris Laboratories said its president and chief executive, Denis Simon, resigned.</p>
<p>Meris announced Simon's appointment on March 25, while disclosing at the same time it had hired a unit of Price Waterhouse to assist in a corporate turnaround.</p>
<p>The announcement of Simon's resignation was released late Friday and attempts to reach the company over the weekend were unsuccessful. The company said in the release that it expects to name a replacement shortly.</p>
<p>Meris Laboratories agreed in February to pay $5.2 million to settle fraud allegations that it filed false claims for reimbursement of laboratory tests under Medicare and Medicaid.</p>
</text>
